The exporter AWS Lambda deployment package bundles the dependencies below.
Bundling is deliberate rather than incidental: the Amazon Connect data tables
API requires boto3 >= 1.35, and the boto3 version present in a Lambda runtime is
whichever version that runtime shipped with. Pinning and bundling makes the
artifact reproducible. The pin is `var.boto3_version` in
modules/flow-exporter/variables.tf.

No dependency below carries a copyleft or otherwise reciprocal licence.

Installed by `pip install boto3==1.42.81`, as resolved on 7 September 2026:

  Package           Version           Licence
  ----------------  ----------------  ------------------------------------------
  boto3             1.42.81           Apache-2.0
  botocore          1.42.97           Apache-2.0
  jmespath          1.1.0             MIT
  python-dateutil   2.9.0.post0       Dual: BSD-3-Clause OR Apache-2.0
  s3transfer        0.16.1            Apache-2.0
  six               1.17.0            MIT
  urllib3           2.7.0             MIT

Note on botocore: the build trims botocore's bundled service definitions to the
five services the exporter actually calls (connect, s3, chime-sdk-voice,
lexv2-models, and the s3transfer dependency's requirements). This reduces the
artifact from roughly 6.1 MB to 1.7 MB. Trimming removes data files only; no
code is modified, so the licence terms above continue to apply unchanged.

